  howpublished = {ICCVW},
  annotation = {中文辅助译名：从情绪到暴力：第九届 ABAW 的多模态细粒度行为分析},
  abstract = {The 9th Affective and Behavior Analysis in-the-Wild (ABAW) Workshop, held in conjunction with ICCV 2025, advances research on modeling, analyzing and understanding human affect and behavior under real-world, unconstrained conditions. Continuing its dual format of competition and paper tracks, the workshop featured three core challenges: Valence-Arousal Estimation, Compound Expression Recognition and Fine-Grained Violence Detection, each designed to benchmark state-of-the-art methods on large-scale in-the-wild datasets. In parallel, the paper track showcased diverse contributions spanning multimodal affect recognition, human-robot interaction, novel datasets, data-centric methodologies, behavior understanding and anomaly detection. Together, these contributions highlight progress in multimodal and multitask learning, cross-domain generalization, privacy-preserving analysis and data efficiency. Building on the success of previous editions, the 9th ABAW Workshop not only provides rigorous benchmarks and curated resources but also strengthens interdisciplinary collaboration across computer vision, AI, psychology, and human-computer interaction, thereby shaping the next generation of human-centered affective computing technologies},
}

